(text
"USB_RAW rising above about 4.455V must remain valid for about 0.2s before USB SYS path turns ON.\nExisting battery path is inhibited immediately by Q606 sensing isolated USB_RAW. Delayed USB turn-on avoids a parallel charge path.\nUSB_RAW falling trips supervisor while Q606 still inhibits the battery; confirm break-before-make on bench.\nPOWER OFF charges battery; POWER ON supplies MCU/AFE from SYS and holds charger CE high.\nLegacy/default-current USB: converter OFF, data works from battery with POWER ON. Type-C 1.5A/3A permits USB-powered flashing without battery.\nUSB-mode minimum pre-LDO headroom and switching noise need validation; external grounded instruments can defeat isolation."
